! mcp_bootstrap_p180.strap -- MCP printed page 180: the tail of the
! operator-message block (the "Z ID" cards), the channel/unit-busy
! retry, and the stacked-interrupt (K 2 INT / RK2INT) test.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.187.  The page's own header was
! READ, not assumed:
!
!   TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID LA000162
!   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  180
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 221040. <<<
! Rendered at 400 dpi with the rest of the heading line; six digits
! follow the word LOCATION, clear of the dashed rule.  Nothing was
! taken off the rule and nothing from the survey OCR.  That is LINE
! 1'S location word (docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1), and line
! 1 here IS a located row (221040.40), which is the case the rule
! predicts to be NUMBERED rather than blank.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPAN, AND WHY THE CACHED SURVEY IS WRONG ABOUT IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIRST LOCATION  221040.40   (line 1)
! LAST  LOCATION  221101.40   (line 51, a half-word branch, so the
!                              counter leaves the page at 221102.00)
! 51 PRINTED LINES.  Nothing fell off either end -- see the card
! serials below, which run unbroken LA000162..LA000207.
!
! The cached survey reports 221041.0 .. 221674.40.  BOTH ENDS ARE
! WRONG and the page's own ink says so:
!   * the low end is one half word late.  Line 1 is 221040.40, read
!     at 900 dpi, and it is confirmed independently by the heading
!     row's LOCATION field (221040) and by printed p.179's own last
!     line (see the backward join).  The survey loses the first row,
!     which docs/transcription_workflow.md says it routinely does.
!   * the high end, 221674.40, is not on this page at all.  The
!     page's largest printed location is 221101.40 and every one of
!     the 51 locations was read at 900 dpi; 221674 is nearly four
!     hundred words past the last row and past several LATER pages
!     (printed p.181 line 20 is 221155.40).  It is noise.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOINS.  THE BACKWARD ONE IS UNUSUALLY STRONG
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 1 IS NOT A WHOLE INSTRUCTION.  IT IS THE OFFSET CARD OF
! AN INSTRUCTION THAT BEGINS ON printed p.179. <<<
!
! Line 1 prints "221040.40   000000.00 87   ,0.0($7)" -- an operation
! field that is EMPTY, which is STRAP's second-card form for the
! offset half word of a VFL instruction (the same shape as printed
! p.138 lines 30-32 and printed p.44 lines 7-16, both landed).
! The instruction's FIRST half word is printed p.179's last line:
!
!   p.179 line 55   221040.00   221050.00 80   ... Z ID01
!
! read out of docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt (the OCR of ANOTHER
! page, which docs/transcription_workflow.md permits as an index and
! forbids as corroboration of this page).  Two things follow and
! both are checkable here:
!   * the counter arrives at 221040.40 exactly, which is this deck's
!     SLC and the heading field's 221040; and
!   * that instruction's address operand is ZID01 at 221050.00,
!     which THIS page defines and this deck's !SYM asserts.  A VFL
!     first half word carries the full 24-bit bit address (measured
!     below), so p.179 reads ZID01 TO THE BIT and agrees.
!
! >>> THE CARD SERIAL CLOSES IT, AND IT CLOSES IT HARDER THAN I
! FIRST WROTE: THE TWO PAGES SHARE ONE CARD. <<<  This page's line 1
! is serial LA000162 and printed p.179's line 56 is ALSO LA000162 --
! one punched card carrying two statements, printing its first line
! at the foot of one page and its second at the head of the next.
! (p.179's last DISTINCT card is LA000161, its lines 54/55.)  A card
! serial is punched, not computed, so a shared serial across a page
! break is a stronger join witness than either location column.
!
! >>> AND printed p.179'S OWN TRANSCRIBER READ IT THE SAME WAY,
! INDEPENDENTLY. <<<  Their deck (in this session's scratchpad, not
! yet in decks/) ends:
!
!   !CHECK 221040.00 | 221050.00 80 | line 56 ,Z ID01 -- A NULL
!   OPERATION ... LAST ROW OF THE PAGE, a HALF WORD, so THE COUNTER
!   LEAVES AT 221040.40, which is what printed p.180 must print
!
! Two transcribers, two renders, two pages of ink, one answer.  The
! backward join is MEASURED, not asserted.  Note the shape they
! settled on: p.179's card writes the ADDRESS half (",Z ID01") and
! this page's line 1 writes the OFFSET half (",0.0($7)"), both with
! an empty operation field.
!
! >>> FORWARD PREDICTION FOR printed p.181, MADE AND THEN TESTED.
! <<<  Line 51 is a half-word branch at 221101.40, so the counter
! leaves this page at 221102.00 and p.181's first LOCATED row must
! be there.  printed p.181's deck landed in this session's
! scratchpad after the prediction was written and says: "THE CODE IS
! CONTIGUOUS FROM 221102.00", its line 4 "B CWC R" at 221102.00
! (lines 1-3 are an asterisk banner), backed by two landed decks
! that already SYN "BCWCR ... (8)221102.0".  CONFIRMED.
!
! THE SERIAL HALF OF THAT PREDICTION WAS WRONG AND IS WORTH
! RECORDING AS SUCH: I expected LA000208 and printed p.181's first
! card is LB000001.  The LA deck ENDS with this page.  So a serial
! run does not have to carry across a page break even when the
! storage does, and "the next page continues the serial" is not a
! rule -- printed p.176/p.175 happened to, and p.180/p.181 do not.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN -- READ, AND COUNTED BY MACHINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 51 printed lines, 46 distinct serials LA000162..LA000207 with NO
! gap (46 = 207-162+1, counted).  FIVE CARDS CARRY TWO STATEMENTS
! and therefore print two lines each:
!
!   LA000188  lines 27/28   K C BUSY V-I,2,2.      ; B,K CH OP N
!   LA000190  lines 30/31   SIC,S DISIC            ; B,S DISP
!   LA000191  lines 32/33   K2INT SVA,$13,RK2INT   ; LV,$13,SFIAAC($12)
!   LA000192  lines 34/35   LVI,$1,$+1.0           ; B,KSERCH
!   LA000198  lines 41/42   KVI,$3,SFREE           ; BXE,RK2INT
!
! 46 + 5 = 51.  Note LA000190: a SIC and its mandatory half-word
! branch punched on ONE card, which is the pairing printed p.176
! argued was a punching style rather than an assembler requirement.
! This page is a second instance of it.
!
! The serials also say the brief's rule holds here: the second
! letter is A, never I or O, over the whole run.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE "K NI" QUESTION THE CALLER ASKED.  ANSWER: NO, AND THE
! DEFINING PAGE IS printed p.177, WHICH DEFINES **BOTH** NAMES. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.167 carries "B,KNI+1.0" printing 220727.50 and could not
! find KNI defined anywhere, guessing its defining page was near
! here.  THIS PAGE DOES NOT DEFINE IT.  What this page has is a
! DIFFERENT symbol:
!
!   p.180 line 46   221077.00   220735.10 00   B,K K NI
!
! read at 900 dpi: K, blank, K, blank, N, I -- "K K NI", which STRAP
! strips to KKNI, at 220735.0 (half word; a branch).  That is NOT
! KNI at 220726.40; the two are seven words apart.
!
! The volume OCR of PDF p.184 = printed p.177 (another page's ink, so
! an index, not corroboration) prints that page's lines 42 and 51 as:
!
!   42*  220726.40 *  000013.47 04   K NI     KVI,3,11.32  -TEST IF WAIT, CHEX OR S FREE
!   51*  220735.00     ...  .45 30   K K NI   SV,2,S ACT AD($13)  -ACTUATED ADDR TO FILE AREA
!
! 220726.40 is exactly p.167's KNI and 220735.00 is exactly this
! page's KKNI -- ONE PAGE DEFINING BOTH NAMES, nine words apart.
!
! >>> AND printed p.177'S OWN DECK, WHICH LANDED IN THIS SESSION'S
! SCRATCHPAD WHILE THIS PAGE WAS BEING WRITTEN, CONFIRMS IT FROM THE
! INK. <<<  It declares, in its own words:
!
!   !SYM KNI     220726.40        ! line 42, NAME printed "K NI"
!   !SYM KKNI    220735.00        ! line 51, NAME printed "K K NI"
!
! So p.167's open question is CLOSED and it was never this page or
! p.178: KNI is printed p.177 line 42.  (My first draft said p.178,
! from an off-by-one on the OCR's own "PDF page 184" banner --
! PDF 184 is printed 177, not 178.  Corrected here against the
! deck.)  This page's only contribution is the second name, KKNI,
! which it reads at 220735.00 off a branch and which p.177 defines
! at 220735.00 exactly.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> WHAT THIS PAGE COULD NOT ASSEMBLE: LINE 25'S "DDI". <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 25 prints, in full:
!
!   25*  000000.00+   +00000077      BU,06 ,10   Z RMTCC  DDI(BU,6),(2)111111
!
! and strap_asm REFUSES it:
!
!   line 1: pseudo-operation DDI not implemented by this assembler
!   yet (see strap_asm.py module docstring / C22-6531)
!
! The refusal is an outright AssemblerError, so leaving the printed
! card in the deck would make the WHOLE PAGE assemble nothing and
! check nothing -- the same shape of problem as printed p.166's
! duplicate label, where "let it fail" is not on offer.  So the card
! is CARRIED IN THE LISTING BLOCK WITH NO !CHECK and is not handed
! to the assembler, exactly as printed p.131 did with its orphaned
! SIC.  >>> NO STAND-IN IS WRITTEN.  A SYN WOULD BE A DIFFERENT
! THING: C22-6531 printed p.30 makes DDI "purely definitive" but
! puts its compiled field RIGHT-JUSTIFIED IN A 24-BIT SYMBOL-TABLE
! ENTRY which an immediate operation then takes LEFT-JUSTIFIED out
! of; a SYN defines a bit address and would disagree with both the
! printed location column (000000.00+) and the printed value. <<<
!
! THE LOSS IS BOUNDED, and here is the bound:
!   * DDI OCCUPIES NO STORAGE.  Line 24 is at 221064.00 (a half-word
!     branch) and line 26 is at 221064.40, so the counter does not
!     move across line 25.  Omitting it cannot shift one later row,
!     and the 42 !CHECK rows below prove that by arriving on every
!     printed location after it.
!   * NOTHING ON THIS PAGE REFERENCES Z RMTCC.  All 51 statements
!     were checked for the name; it appears once, as this card's own
!     label.
!   * BUT A NEIGHBOUR DOES REFERENCE IT, AND THE SCOPE OF THAT
!     MATTERS, SO HERE IS EXACTLY WHAT WAS MEASURED.  No deck in
!     decks/ mentions RMTCC (all 156 grepped, zero hits), and the
!     volume OCR of both halves of the listing contains the string
!     exactly ONCE -- at this page's own line 25 (the "S RMTC" and
!     "T RMTC" hits are a different symbol, a reminder-message time
!     constant).  HOWEVER, printed p.179 line 28 is
!     "KI(BU,6),Z RMTCC" at 221016.40, printing 770000.00 80, and
!     the volume OCR garbles the name past recognition there, which
!     is why the grep missed it.  p.179's in-flight deck carries a
!     STAND-IN, "ZRMTCC SYN(BU,6), (2)111111".
!
!     THAT IS WHY THIS DECK WRITES NO STAND-IN OF ITS OWN.  With
!     p.179 defining the name and this page defining nothing, the
!     merged image has EXACTLY ONE definition and cannot collide.
!     Had both pages written a stand-in, the merge would have had
!     two -- the printed-p.157 failure mode in a new costume.
!
!     If anyone later implements DDI, THIS is the card to compile:
!     mode BU, field length 0o06 = 6, byte size 0o10 = 8, value
!     (2)111111 = 0o77 = 63, printed +00000077, and C22-6531
!     printed p.30 says the 24-bit symbol-table entry holds it
!     RIGHT-justified while an immediate operation takes the
!     low-order field out LEFT-justified -- which is exactly the
!     770000.00 p.179 prints.  The two pages are consistent.
!
! That is the one assembler limitation this page hit.  Everything
! else on the page was handed to strap_asm EXACTLY AS PRINTED and
! was accepted: the empty-operation offset card ",0.0($7)", the
! "(IQSX)" entry-mode DDs, "CF,8", "V-I,2,2." with its trailing
! period, "B,$.32" with no plus sign, and "LVI,$13,$".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Three things, in printed order.
!
! (1) Lines 1-14 finish a routine that converts a job name to IQS
!     code and plants it in an operator message.  C22-6728-1 prints
!     the same call sequence in TYPESET prose -- "LVI, 15, $+1. /
!     BD, SA6IQS / VF, YJCDB1+1. / CF, 8 / VF, ..." under the
!     heading "The BCD to IQS Conversion Routine ... entered at
!     SA6IQS or SA8IQS according to the byte size".  This page's
!     lines 5-9 are that sequence with B in place of BD and ZID12 as
!     the destination parameter.  The manual is typeset, so it is a
!     genuinely independent witness for the two names.
!
! (2) Lines 16-22 are the message text itself: seven "(IQSX)DD(BU)"
!     cards spelling "OPERATOR** LOAD / CHANNEL / UNIT WITH / REEL
!     NO. / JOB / PROTECT / **MCP**".
!
! (3) Lines 26-51 are channel/unit code: K C BUSY retries, K NOT AV
!     gives up to the dispatcher, and K 2 INT / RK2INT decides
!     whether a stacked interrupt is a stray.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE "(IQSX)" CARDS: HOW THE BLANKS WERE COUNTED, BY MACHINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Five of the seven have RUNS OF BLANKS inside the datum, and in
! entry mode a blank is DATA (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
! "In entry mode the space after the comma is DATA").  Counting them
! by eye off a drum print is exactly the thing that puts a symbol
! six bits late, so they were counted by pixel instead:
!
!   The statement column was rendered at 800 dpi and every glyph run
!   located.  The listing is 10 characters per inch -- the thirteen
!   glyphs of the constant prefix "(IQSX)DD(BU)," span 964 px, i.e.
!   80.33 px per cell -- so each run's left edge rounds to a
!   character cell with no ambiguity (the worst residual is 0.2 of a
!   cell).  Cell 0 is "(" and cell 12 is the comma; the datum is
!   cells 13..(cell of the terminating X minus 1).
!
!   line  X at cell  datum cells  chars  bits  next printed location
!    16      29         13..28      16    128   221052.00  (+2 words)
!    17      21         13..20       8     64   221053.00  (+1 word)
!    18      29         13..28      16    128   221055.00  (+2 words)
!    19      22         13..21       9     72   221056.10  (+1 word + 8)
!    20      28         13..27      15    120   221060.00
!    21      29         13..28      16    128   221062.00  (+2 words)
!    22      21         13..20       8     64   221063.00  (+1 word)
!
! ALL SEVEN AGREE WITH THE PRINTED LOCATION COLUMN at eight bits per
! character, which is the dds's own default: no byte size is written,
! and C28-6129 printed p.16 makes a null byte size eight ("byte size
! is treated modulo 8").  The 9-character "REEL NO. " is the row that
! makes this a measurement rather than a convention -- it is the only
! one that lands OFF a word boundary, at 221056.10, and ZID04 is
! defined there.
!
! >>> AND printed p.179 CONFIRMS THAT ODD OFFSET FROM OUTSIDE. <<<
! The volume OCR of p.179 line 44 is "221031.00  221056.10+  VF,Z ID
! 04" -- a VF, which prints its operand's FULL 24-bit bit address
! (measured below).  So another page, another card, reads ZID04 at
! 221056.10 to the bit.  Had this page's "REEL NO. " been read as 8
! or 10 characters, ZID04 would be at 221056.00 or 221056.20 and
! that row would disagree.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHICH EXTERNALS ARE READ TO THE BIT AND WHICH ARE NOT -- MEASURED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Run through strap_asm, varying ONLY the SYN's bit offset over
! .00/.01/.37/.40/.41 and nothing else, for the operations this page
! actually uses:
!
!   TI,2,X,Y   first operand   230567.00 | .01 | .37 | .40 | .41
!   L(BU,4),X($13) 1st half    230567.00 | .01 | .37 | .40 | .41
!   VF,X+1.0                   230570.00 | .01 | .37 | .40 | .41
!   SIC,X                      (p.176: every bit shows)
!   ---- everything below collapses to TWO values ----
!   LV,$13,X($12)              230567.32 | .32 | .32 | .72 | .72
!   LVI,14,X                   230567.35 | .35 | .35 | .75 | .75
!   SVA,7,X                    230567.17 | .17 | .17 | .57 | .57
!   SV,2,X                     230567.05 | .05 | .05 | .45 | .45
!   KVI,3,X                    230567.07 | .07 | .07 | .47 | .47
!   B,X                        230567.10 | .10 | .10 | .50 | .50
!   TI,2,X,Y   second operand  221055.04 | .04 | .04 | .44 | .44
!
! So on THIS page the bit-exact readings are KSCRAC (a TI first
! operand), SIOIND (an L first half word), YJCDB1 (a VF) and SDISIC
! (a SIC).  Every other external is known to the HALF WORD only, and
! each is marked below.  Writing ".0" for those is a CONVENTION.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK: EXACTLY THREE, COUNTED BY MACHINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All 51 line numbers carry the ordinary asterisk ("1*" .. "51*").
! A SECOND asterisk, after the LOCATION, appears on exactly three
! rows.  Counted rather than eyeballed: the page was rendered at 400
! dpi, banded on the LINE-number column's own ink (52 bands -- the
! heading row and the 51 lines, which is a third independent
! confirmation of the row count), and the dark pixels counted per
! band in the asterisk column:
!
!   line 13   221047.00 *   LVI,7,10.0        287 dark px
!   line 22   221062.00 *   (IQSX)DD(BU)...   256 dark px
!   line 44   221076.00 *   BZRZ,Z E4         273 dark px
!   all other 48 rows: 0
!   (line 25's ink two cells to the LEFT is the "+" of its
!    "000000.00+" DDI location, not an asterisk)
!
! I OFFER NO RULE.  docs/transcription_workflow.md says not to
! propose one from a single page and names the page that killed the
! last attempt.  The three rows here have nothing in common I can
! see: a LVI, a DD and a branch; one of them is the only DD of the
! seven to be marked.  Recorded and left.
!
! ONE MORE MARK, NOT AN ASTERISK: line 30 (SIC,S DISIC) carries a
! single small tick in the NAME column, about the size of an
! apostrophe and well above the baseline.  printed p.176 line 21 has
! the same thing and reached the same conclusion: it is not an
! asterisk and it is not a name.  Recorded.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS DOUBTFUL AND WHAT SETTLED IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs constantly and says so in its own
! heading, which prints "LOCATICN" for LOCATION and "BINARY CUTPUT"
! for OUTPUT, and in its time clock, which prints "00054041" as
! "C0054041".  In the body, "215265.05" prints ".C5", "230567.50"
! prints ".5C", and "010003.35" prints "C1CC03.35".  EVERY ONE OF
! THOSE IS AN OCTAL FIELD, so every one of those C's is a 0 with
! certainty (rung 5).  The four that actually mattered:
!
!   "YJCDB1" (line 7).  C or O?  B or 8?  Settled on rung 2, the
!   typeset manuals: C22-6728-1 prints "YJCDB1", "YJCDBU" and
!   "YBCBU" -- four hits for JCDB, ZERO for JODB.  The character
!   after B is "1" and not "I": at 1600 dpi it has the 1's angled
!   top-left flag and no top/bottom bars, against the unmistakable
!   barred I's of "IQSX" on the same page.
!
!   "SA6IQS" (line 6).  TWELVE typeset hits across the two revisions
!   of C22-6728 (7 in -1, 5 in the base), which also print the whole
!   calling sequence; ZERO typeset hits for any other spelling.  The
!   Q's tail is clean at 1600 dpi.
!
!   >>> AND THIS DISAGREES WITH printed p.179, WHICH READS THE SAME
!   WORD "SA6IGS". <<<  Both pages branch to 230567.40 and both
!   print the same card shape.  Run through
!   tests/check_symbol_spellings.py over the landed corpus plus both
!   new decks, it is reported as "two spellings of one symbol at
!   5004768: SA6IGS (pp.179) vs SA6IQS (pp.180) -- glyph G/Q".
!   THE EVIDENCE IS ONE-SIDED: the ONLY occurrence of "SA6IGS" in
!   any document in docs/ocr/ is a single hit in
!   MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, i.e. the OCR of THIS LISTING -- same drum,
!   worse reader, which docs/transcription_workflow.md disqualifies
!   as a witness.  Against it stand twelve typeset hits in a
!   different document set off a different press.  p.179's deck
!   should read SA6IQS at its lines 91, 414, 478, 556 and 557.
!
!   "010003" (line 29, S CH NAV).  Four round glyphs in a six-digit
!   OCTAL word address, so all four are 0.  Independently: printed
!   p.107's landed deck already defines "SCHNAV SYN,(16)1003.0", and
!   (16)1003 = 0o10003.  Agreement between a hex SYN on one page and
!   an octal print on another is about as independent as this corpus
!   gets.
!
!   "Q INT" in line 43's comment (-OTHERWISE, TEST IF Q INT IS CS).
!   G/Q is the sixth pair this drum confuses.  Rendered at 1600 dpi
!   beside this page's own "K ASIGN" (line 47's NAME), the two are
!   different: the G carries a horizontal bar at MID height on the
!   inside of the bowl, and this glyph's stroke is a diagonal at the
!   BOTTOM right that projects OUTSIDE the bowl -- a Q's tail, the
!   same shape as the Q of "SA6IQS" two dozen rows above.  NOTHING
!   RESTS ON IT: it is comment text, it touches no bit and no
!   symbol, and the deck records it only so the next reader knows it
!   was looked at rather than copied.
!
!   "B,$.32" (line 36).  There is NO plus sign -- rendered at 1600
!   dpi the glyphs are B , $ . 3 2 with a clean gap where a "+"
!   would be.  Noted because the assembler cannot tell: "$+.32"
!   compiles the same word, so this is an ink reading and rung 3 is
!   silent on it.
!
! The mnemonics took rung 3 (hand both readings to the assembler) in
! two places and it fired: "BZRZ" and "BZXE" are operations and
! their O-for-C neighbours are not.  No DR/DRZ anywhere on the page,
! so the reservation blindness does not arise.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS ASSERTED, AND HERE IS WHAT BACKS IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  Line 1 is a located row, so this
! deck writes a hard "SLC, (8)221040.40", and
! docs/transcription_workflow.md item 2 applies: a hard SLC cannot
! disagree with an arriving counter, it overrides it silently.  The
! 42 !CHECK rows below therefore ASSERT this origin rather than
! check it.  Three independent things back it:
!   THE WORD, 221040, is the heading row's own LOCATION field.
!   THE HALF WORD, .40, is printed p.179's line 55 occupying
!     221040.00 as the first half of the instruction whose offset
!     card is this page's line 1.
!   THE REST OF THE PAGE then lands: every one of the 51 printed
!     locations follows from this origin with no fudge, including
!     the 8-bit-offset DD at 221056.10 and the CNOP at line 15 that
!     prints no location at all.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CNOP (line 15) EMITS NOTHING, AND THE PAGE SAYS SO
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 15 prints "15*" and then a BLANK location and a BLANK binary
! column.  Line 14 is a half-word branch at 221047.40, so the
! counter is already at 221050.00 -- full-word aligned -- and
! C22-6531's CNOP has nothing to bridge.  strap_asm models exactly
! that (a zero-size, full-word-aligned statement) and the deck
! writes the printed CNOP; ZID01 then lands at 221050.00, which the
! !SYM below checks.  This is NOT a hole in the image: no word is
! skipped anywhere on this page, there is no DR/DRZ and no forward
! SLC, and the storage runs contiguously from 221040.40 to
! 221101.77.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  Every one is SYN'd from a LANDED deck's reading where
! one exists, and this page's own printed word is quoted beside it
! as the check.  "HALF WORD ONLY" marks the ones whose bit offset
! this page cannot see (see the measurement table above).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! printed "S TIC".  Defined printed
                                     ! p.116 line 16 "S T IC VF,0".
                                     ! Lines 2 and 50 print 215265.05;
                                     ! an SV sees the HALF WORD ONLY,
                                     ! but printed p.176's 24 SICs pin
                                     ! STIC to the bit at .00.
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! printed "K SUPP".  Defined printed
                                     ! p.128.  Lines 3 and 51 print
                                     ! 216242.10 -- HALF WORD ONLY.
SA6IQS  SYN, (8)230567.40            ! printed "SA6IQS", line 6, 230567.50.
                                     ! The .40 (bit 32) IS observed; the
                                     ! bits below it are not -- HALF WORD
                                     ! ONLY.  C22-6728-1 names the routine
                                     ! in typeset prose (12 hits).
YJCDB1  SYN, (8)231443.0             ! printed "YJCDB1", line 7's
                                     ! "VF,YJCDB1+1.0" = 231444.00+.
                                     ! A VF prints the FULL 24-bit value,
                                     ! so this is BIT-EXACT: any non-zero
                                     ! offset would print in the .00.
KSCRAC  SYN, (8)222013.0             ! printed "KSCRAC", line 23's TI first
                                     ! operand, 222013.00 -- BIT-EXACT.
                                     ! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p166.strap
                                     ! already carries this same SYN.
SCHNAV  SYN,(16)1003.0               ! printed "S CH NAV", line 29's
                                     ! 010003.35.  (16)1003 = 0o10003.
                                     ! Spelling and value both taken from
                                     ! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap,
                                     ! which DEFINES it ("- 3 CHANNEL NOT
                                     ! AVAILABLE").  HALF WORD ONLY here.
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! printed "S DISIC", line 30's
                                     ! "SIC,S DISIC" = 217451.40 80.
                                     ! A SIC is BIT-EXACT.  Eighteen
                                     ! landed decks carry the same value.
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! printed "S DISP", line 31's
                                     ! 217372.10 -- HALF WORD ONLY.
                                     ! Seventeen landed decks agree.
SFIAAC  SYN(BU,18), 3.0              ! printed "SFIAAC", line 33.  THE dds
                                     ! IS CARRIED FROM THE DEFINING PAGE
                                     ! (printed p.101 line 13, "-FILE AREA
                                     ! ACTIVATED"), per the merge rule --
                                     ! this page's LV writes no dds and
                                     ! would otherwise take its length
                                     ! from the symbol.  HALF WORD ONLY.
KSERCH  SYN, (8)222020.0             ! printed "KSERCH", line 35's
                                     ! 222020.10 -- HALF WORD ONLY.
DREL    SYN, 2.32                    ! printed "D REL", line 37's
                                     ! 000002.47 (0o40 + 2J+1 for J=3).
                                     ! DEFINED printed p.104 line 12 with
                                     ! no dds.  HALF WORD ONLY.
DFREE   SYN, 10.32                   ! printed "D FREE", line 39's
                                     ! 000012.47.  Defined printed p.104
                                     ! line 44.  (The "DFREE SYN, 0" in
                                     ! pp.71/75/97/98 is the OTHER
                                     ! assembly, pp.15-98.)  HALF WORD.
SFREE   SYN, 12.32                   ! printed "SFREE" on line 41 and
                                     ! "S FREE" on line 47 -- two cards,
                                     ! one symbol, and both print
                                     ! 000014.47, which is this page's own
                                     ! proof that the blank is nothing.
                                     ! Defined printed p.105 line 1.
SIOIND  SYN(BU,5), 1.09              ! printed "S IO IND", line 43's
                                     ! 000001.11 8D.  An L's first half
                                     ! word is BIT-EXACT, and 0o11 = 9 is
                                     ! exactly printed p.102 line 7's
                                     ! "SIOIND SYN(BU,5), 1.09".  The dds
                                     ! is carried from that defining page
                                     ! although this row overrules it with
                                     ! its own (BU,4).
ZE2     SYN, (8)221155.40            ! printed "Z E2", line 48's
                                     ! 221155.72 (0o40 + indicator 0o32).
                                     ! HALF WORD ONLY.  DEFINED printed
                                     ! p.182 line 20, whose own deck
                                     ! declares !SYM ZE2 221155.40.
ZE4     SYN, (8)221157.0             ! printed "Z E4", line 44's
                                     ! 221157.34 (indicator 0o34, bit 32
                                     ! CLEAR).  HALF WORD ONLY.  DEFINED
                                     ! printed p.182 line 23, !SYM ZE4
                                     ! 221157.00.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE IS THE ONE printed p.182 ASKED FOR. <<<  Its deck's
! "WHAT IS NOT SETTLED" says of ZE1..ZE4: "no other landed deck
! references any of them, so no merge, no oracle and no spelling
! check can ever confirm their names ... A page that branches to one
! of these would settle the spelling."  THIS PAGE BRANCHES TO TWO OF
! THEM, from a different card deck (LA vs LC) on a different page:
! line 48 BZXE,Z E2 -> 221155.40 and line 44 BZRZ,Z E4 -> 221157.00,
! both agreeing with p.182's !SYMs to the half word.  The NAMES are
! still two readings of the same drum, but they are now two
! INDEPENDENT readings on two pages, and the two ADDRESSES are
! cross-checked by the merge the moment both decks land.
KKNI    SYN, (8)220735.0             ! printed "K K NI", line 46's
                                     ! 220735.10.  HALF WORD ONLY.
                                     ! >>> NOT "KNI", which is a DIFFERENT
                                     ! symbol at 220726.40 (printed p.167
                                     ! reads it off a branch).  BOTH are
                                     ! defined on printed p.177, whose deck
                                     ! declares !SYM KKNI 220735.00 -- see
                                     ! the note at the head of this file.
ZID07   SYN, (8)221035.40            ! printed "Z ID 07", line 14's
                                     ! 221035.50.  HALF WORD ONLY.  Back
                                     ! reference to printed p.179, whose
                                     ! OCR shows "ZID07 SIC,KCONVR" at
                                     ! 221035.40.
ZID08   SYN, (8)221035.0             ! printed "Z ID08", line 12's
                                     ! 221035.10.  HALF WORD ONLY.  p.179
                                     ! OCR: "Z ID08 LVI,9,20" at 221035.00.
ZID09A  SYN, (8)221031.40            ! printed "Z ID09A", line 24's
                                     ! 221031.50.  HALF WORD ONLY.  p.179
                                     ! OCR has "Z ID09A BB,SOWNER($11),Z
                                     ! ID15" at 221031.40 -- and that row's
                                     ! own operand reads THIS page's ZID15
                                     ! at 221045.40, which the !SYM below
                                     ! asserts.

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN.  The page prints no SLC; see the note above.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)221040.40

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE.  Statements are the PRINTED ones.  Where the printed
! NAME or operand carries blanks, STRAP ignores them and the deck
! writes the name closed up, with the printed spelling in the
! comment (the house convention -- see decks/mcp_bootstrap_p168).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        ,0.0($7)                     ! line  1  the OFFSET CARD of printed
                                     !          p.179 line 55's instruction
KCHOPN  SV,2,STIC                    ! line  2  printed "K CHOP N" / "S TIC"
        B,KSUPP                      ! line  3  printed "B,K SUPP"
                                     !          -LOOP TO ACTUATED ADDRESS
ZID09   SVA,7,ZID12                  ! line  4  printed "Z ID09" / "Z ID12"
        LVI,15,$+1.0                 ! line  5
        B,SA6IQS                     ! line  6  -CONVERT JOB NAME
        VF,YJCDB1+1.0                ! line  7
        CF,8                         ! line  8
ZID12   VF,0.0                       ! line  9  printed "Z ID12"
ZID09X  B,0.0                        ! line 10  printed "Z ID09X"; printed
                                     !          p.166 line 22 SICs this
                                     !          symbol, which pins it to
                                     !          the bit at 221045.00
ZID15   TI,1,ZID16,ZID04A            ! line 11  printed "Z ID 15" /
                                     !          "Z ID16" / "Z ID04A"
        B,ZID08                      ! line 12  printed "B,Z ID08"
ZID13   LVI,7,10.0                   ! line 13  printed "Z ID 13" *
        B,ZID07                      ! line 14  printed "B,Z ID 07"
        CNOP                         ! line 15  emits nothing: the counter
                                     !          is already at 221050.00
ZID01   (IQSX)DD(BU),OPERATOR** LOAD X     ! line 16  16 chars, 128 bits
ZID02   (IQSX)DD(BU),CHANNEL X             ! line 17   8 chars,  64 bits
ZID02A  (IQSX)DD(BU),   UNIT   WITH  X     ! line 18  16 chars, 128 bits
ZID03   (IQSX)DD(BU),REEL NO. X            ! line 19   9 chars,  72 bits
ZID04   (IQSX)DD(BU),           JOB X      ! line 20  15 chars, 120 bits
ZID04A  (IQSX)DD(BU),         PROTECTX     ! line 21  16 chars, 128 bits
ZID16   (IQSX)DD(BU), **MCP**X             ! line 22   8 chars,  64 bits *
ZID14   TI,2,KSCRAC,ZID03            ! line 23  printed "Z ID14"
        B,ZID09A                     ! line 24  printed "B,Z ID09A"
!       line 25 IS NOT HERE.  "Z RMTCC DDI(BU,6),(2)111111" --
!       strap_asm refuses DDI outright and would assemble NOTHING.
!       It occupies no storage, so the counter is unaffected; see the
!       note at the head of this file for the full printed card and
!       the bound on what is lost.
ZRENME  VF,0.34                      ! line 26  printed "Z RENME"
KCBUSY  V-I,2,2.                     ! line 27  printed "K C BUSY"; the
                                     !          trailing period is printed
        B,KCHOPN                     ! line 28  printed "B,K CH OP N" --
                                     !          same symbol as line 2's
                                     !          "K CHOP N", and this page
                                     !          proves it: 221041.10
KNOTAV  LVI,14,SCHNAV                ! line 29  printed "K NOT AV" /
                                     !          "S CH NAV"
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 30  printed "SIC,S DISIC";
                                     !          a tick in the NAME column
        B,SDISP                      ! line 31  printed "B,S DISP"
K2INT   SVA,$13,RK2INT               ! line 32
        LV,$13,SFIAAC($12)           ! line 33
        LVI,$1,$+1.0                 ! line 34
        B,KSERCH                     ! line 35
        B,$.32                       ! line 36  NO plus sign is printed
        KVI,3,DREL                   ! line 37  printed "D REL"
                                     !          -IF $REL OR $FREE, DISCARD
        BXE,RK2INT                   ! line 38
        KVI,3,DFREE                  ! line 39  printed "D FREE"
        BXE,RK2INT                   ! line 40
        KVI,$3,SFREE                 ! line 41  printed "$3" here and "3"
                                     !          on line 47: same word
        BXE,RK2INT                   ! line 42
        L(BU,4),SIOIND($13)          ! line 43  printed "S IO IND"
                                     !          -OTHERWISE, TEST IF Q INT
                                     !           IS CS
        BZRZ,ZE4                     ! line 44  printed "Z E4" *
                                     !          -IF NOT CS, THROW HIM OFF
RK2INT  LVI,$13,$                    ! line 45
        B,KKNI                       ! line 46  printed "B,K K NI"
                                     !          -IF CS (STRAY), PROCEED
KASIGN  KVI,3,SFREE                  ! line 47  printed "K ASIGN" /
                                     !          "S FREE"  -TEST IF S FREE
        BZXE,ZE2                     ! line 48  printed "Z E2"
        V+I,2,1.32                   ! line 49
        SV,2,STIC                    ! line 50  -IF SO, NOP
        B,KSUPP                      ! line 51

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DECLARED CHECKS.  20 symbols against the LOCATION column and
! 42 rows against the BINARY OUTPUT column -- every printed row that
! emits anything except line 25's refused DDI.  Lines 15-22 emit
! character data and print no BINARY OUTPUT, so they are checked by
! their LOCATIONS (!SYM) instead, which is the whole of what the
! page prints for them.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM KCHOPN 221041.00
!SYM ZID09  221042.00
!SYM ZID12  221044.40
!SYM ZID09X 221045.00
!SYM ZID15  221045.40
!SYM ZID13  221047.00
!SYM ZID01  221050.00
!SYM ZID02  221052.00
!SYM ZID02A 221053.00
!SYM ZID03  221055.00
!SYM ZID04  221056.10
!SYM ZID04A 221060.00
!SYM ZID16  221062.00
!SYM ZID14  221063.00
!SYM ZRENME 221064.40
!SYM KCBUSY 221065.00
!SYM KNOTAV 221066.00
!SYM K2INT  221067.40
!SYM RK2INT 221076.40
!SYM KASIGN 221077.40

!CHECK 221040.40 | 000000.00 87 | line  1 ,0.0($7) -- the offset half word of printed p.179 line 55's VFL instruction; 87's low nibble 7 is the index $7 and the 000000.00 is offset zero
!CHECK 221041.00 | 215265.05 30 | line  2 K CHOP N SV,2,S TIC -- .05 is 2J+1 for J=2 and is no part of S TIC's offset, so this row checks the HALF WORD only
!CHECK 221041.40 | 216242.10 00 | line  3 B,K SUPP -- 0o10 is the branch, bit 32 clear, so K SUPP is at 216242.00 to the half word
!CHECK 221042.00 | 221044.57 D0 | line  4 Z ID09 SVA,7,Z ID12 -- Z ID12 is 221044.40 on THIS page, so .40 + 2J+1 = 0o17 gives 0o57; an internal reference, a real check of placement
!CHECK 221042.40 | 221043.77 01 | line  5 LVI,15,$+1.0 -- $ is 221042.40 so the target is 221043.40; 0o40 + 2J+1 = 0o37 gives 0o77
!CHECK 221043.00 | 230567.50 00 | line  6 B,SA6IQS -- 0o50 = 0o40 + the branch's 0o10, so SA6IQS is at 230567.40; C22-6728-1 prints the same calling sequence in typeset
!CHECK 221043.40 | 231444.00+ | line  7 VF,YJCDB1+1.0 -- a VF prints the whole 24-bit value, so this row reads YJCDB1 TO THE BIT at 231443.00
!CHECK 221044.00 | 000010 | line  8 CF,8 -- a count field, 18 bits in positions 0-17, printed as six octal digits with no bit position and no hex byte
!CHECK 221044.40 | 000000.00+ | line  9 Z ID12 VF,0.0 -- the destination parameter of the IQS conversion call, planted zero
!CHECK 221045.00 | 000000.10 00 | line 10 Z ID09X B,0.0 -- a branch to zero, filled in at run time; printed p.166 line 22 SICs this label
!CHECK 221045.40 | 221062.00 80 221060.02 A0 | line 11 Z ID 15 TI,1,Z ID16,Z ID04A -- both operands are defined on THIS page (221062.00 and 221060.00) so both halves check placement; the .02 is the count 1
!CHECK 221046.40 | 221035.10 00 | line 12 B,Z ID08 -- bit 32 clear, Z ID08 at 221035.00 on printed p.179
!CHECK 221047.00 | 000012.17 01 | line 13 Z ID 13 LVI,7,10.0 -- 10 decimal is 0o12 and 2J+1 = 0o17; the row carries a SECOND asterisk after its location
!CHECK 221047.40 | 221035.50 00 | line 14 B,Z ID 07 -- 0o50 = 0o40 + 0o10, so Z ID07 is at 221035.40, the half word after Z ID08
!CHECK 221063.00 | 222013.00 80 221055.04 A0 | line 23 Z ID14 TI,2,KSCRAC,ZID03 -- the TI's FIRST operand is a full 24-bit bit address, so KSCRAC is read to the bit at 222013.00; ZID03 is this page's own 221055.00 and the .04 is the count 2
!CHECK 221064.00 | 221031.50 00 | line 24 B,Z ID09A -- 0o50 = 0o40 + 0o10, Z ID09A at 221031.40 on printed p.179
!CHECK 221064.40 | 000000.42+ | line 26 Z RENME VF,0.34 -- 34 DECIMAL is 0o42; written decimal exactly as the statement column prints it
!CHECK 221065.00 | 000002.05 0D | line 27 K C BUSY V-I,2,2. -- word 2 with the trailing period the card prints, and .05 = 2J+1 for J=2
!CHECK 221065.40 | 221041.10 00 | line 28 B,K CH OP N -- an INTERNAL back reference to line 2's "K CHOP N" at 221041.00, which is what proves the two spacings are one symbol
!CHECK 221066.00 | 010003.35 01 | line 29 K NOT AV LVI,14,S CH NAV -- 0o10003 = (16)1003, printed p.107's definition; .35 is 2J+1 for J=14 and bit 32 is clear
!CHECK 221066.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 30 SIC,S DISIC -- a SIC carries the operand's full 24-bit bit address, so S DISIC is read TO THE BIT at 217451.40
!CHECK 221067.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 31 B,S DISP -- the branch half of line 30's card (both are LA000190); HALF WORD only
!CHECK 221067.40 | 221076.73 D0 | line 32 K2INT SVA,$13,RK2INT -- RK2INT is 221076.40 on this page, so 0o40 + 2J+1 = 0o33 gives 0o73; a real placement check
!CHECK 221070.00 | 000003.32 3C | line 33 LV,$13,SFIAAC($12) -- SFIAAC is 3.0 (printed p.101) and .32 is 2J = 26 for J=13; 3C's low nibble C is the index $12
!CHECK 221070.40 | 221071.43 01 | line 34 LVI,$1,$+1.0 -- $ is 221070.40 so the target is 221071.40; 0o40 + 2J+1 = 3 gives 0o43
!CHECK 221071.00 | 222020.10 00 | line 35 B,KSERCH -- HALF WORD only
!CHECK 221071.40 | 221072.10 00 | line 36 B,$.32 -- $ is 221071.40 and 32 DECIMAL more is 221072.00; printed with NO plus sign, which only the ink can say because $+.32 compiles the same word
!CHECK 221072.00 | 000002.47 04 | line 37 KVI,3,D REL -- D REL is 2.32 decimal (printed p.104), so 0o40 + 2J+1 = 0o07 gives 0o47
!CHECK 221072.40 | 221076.72 C2 | line 38 BXE,RK2INT -- 0o72 = 0o40 + indicator 0o32 (XE), and RK2INT at 221076.40 is on this page
!CHECK 221073.00 | 000012.47 04 | line 39 KVI,3,D FREE -- D FREE is 10.32 decimal = 0o12.40 (printed p.104 line 44)
!CHECK 221073.40 | 221076.72 C2 | line 40 BXE,RK2INT -- the same word as lines 38 and 42, printed three times on this page in the same character positions
!CHECK 221074.00 | 000014.47 04 | line 41 KVI,$3,SFREE -- S FREE is 12.32 decimal = 0o14.40 (printed p.105 line 1)
!CHECK 221074.40 | 221076.72 C2 | line 42 BXE,RK2INT -- same card as line 41 (LA000198)
!CHECK 221075.00 | 000001.11 8D 004000.20 50 | line 43 L(BU,4),S IO IND($13) -- an L's first half word is the full 24-bit bit address, so S IO IND is read TO THE BIT at 1.09 decimal = 0o1.11, exactly printed p.102's SYN; 8D's low nibble D is the index $13 and 50 is the LOAD
!CHECK 221076.00 | 221157.34 C0 | line 44 BZRZ,Z E4 -- indicator 0o34 with bit 32 CLEAR, so Z E4 is at 221157.00; the row carries a SECOND asterisk after its location
!CHECK 221076.40 | 221076.73 01 | line 45 RK2INT LVI,$13,$ -- $ is the row's own 221076.40, so 0o40 + 2J+1 = 0o33 gives 0o73; a self-reference and the strongest check of this symbol
!CHECK 221077.00 | 220735.10 00 | line 46 B,K K NI -- bit 32 clear, K K NI at 220735.00.  NOT the K NI of printed p.167 (220726.40); both are defined on printed p.177, whose deck declares !SYM KKNI 220735.00
!CHECK 221077.40 | 000014.47 04 | line 47 K ASIGN KVI,3,S FREE -- the IDENTICAL word to line 41, which the page prints with "SFREE" closed up and here with "S FREE" open: one symbol, two spacings, one word
!CHECK 221100.00 | 221155.72 C0 | line 48 BZXE,Z E2 -- 0o72 = 0o40 + indicator 0o32, so Z E2 is at 221155.40; printed p.181's own OCR labels 221155.40 "Z E2"
!CHECK 221100.40 | 000001.45 05 | line 49 V+I,2,1.32 -- 32 DECIMAL is 0o40, plus 2J+1 = 0o05
!CHECK 221101.00 | 215265.05 30 | line 50 SV,2,S TIC -- the same word as line 2, printed twice on this page
!CHECK 221101.40 | 216242.10 00 | line 51 B,K SUPP -- the same word as line 3; the last row of the page, a half word, so the counter leaves at 221102.00

